{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"fa7cd076f91718d25e1bf19722548c555d54af3152a15cd3ede61cbe8e82094e","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_435e1359fb197873dc3883ff85c2ec2dc767955d4a4a167dd0e6b5248eba8dff","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a method for unsupervised perceptual reward learning for robotic manipulation. The supplied evidence is insufficient to determine specific policy compliance regarding anonymity, plagiarism, or broader impact documentation, as no frozen venue policies or external overlap data are available. The paper does not contain explicit ethical risk assessments, data privacy statements, or consent documentation for the human demonstrations used in the experiments.","paper_id":"Bkul3t9ee","paper_identity_sha256":"c7ce89754ea00dd908466877977582e61c09190a57e8b9796025a12f917d366a","prompt_identity_sha256":"0cc92e67283e60df4894b657d2cc8b65ed30ce73898530969d3c3b9589b44788","raw_response_sha256":"6b3042af33f8f7f6e15c12964eb3a40a3f69945a220c7dfa66cfa6c3f452782a","request_identity_sha256":"c310bd272618fadc043c3fa13db60f66c3623e3ba06af0953fb6f5a0e6923395","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"11a8a2a472bd3f1bcb618fd551d9a76ef0030fbdfef61d15e8f9cddb11868c72","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not contain a dedicated section or explicit discussion regarding ethical risks, fairness, bias, or potential harms associated with the deployment of the proposed robotic learning method. The focus is primarily on the technical efficacy of the reward learning algorithm. No material ethical-risk pathway, such as concrete harm to populations or dual-use concerns, is addressed in the text.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-018","SRC-025","SRC-027"],"review_text":"The paper states that training videos were collected using a smartphone and that demonstrations were provided by humans (SRC-018, SRC-025, SRC-027). However, the text does not provide details on data consent, privacy protections, or whether the human demonstrators were informed about the use of their video data. There is no mention of anonymization of the human subjects in the video data or compliance with specific data usage regulations.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001","SRC-030"],"review_text":"The paper explicitly lists the authors (Pierre Sermanet, Kelvin Xu, Sergey Levine), their affiliation (Google Brain), and their email addresses (SRC-001). The acknowledgments section also names specific individuals (Vincent Vanhoucke, Mrinal Kalakrishnan, Ali Yahya) (SRC-030). Without a frozen venue anonymity policy for the specific submission context, these visible identifiers cannot be declared as a policy violation, but they are present in the text.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The supplied evidence does not include external plagiarism checks, overlap analysis, or information regarding dual submission. The paper cites prior work appropriately in the references and related work sections. Absence of evidence in the provided text does not prove originality or the absence of dual submission; therefore, no judgment on plagiarism or dual submission can be made based solely on the supplied paper text.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement, a responsible AI checklist, or explicit documentation of IRB/ethics approvals. There is no mention of software or data licensing terms for the released code or datasets. Without a frozen policy obligation requiring these specific documents for this venue and year, the absence of these items is noted as a lack of visible compliance documentation rather than a violation.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"e43